  "caption": "Saturday footy: Quinn tackled shoulder-first, felt an electric zap down one arm, and a minute later wanted back on.\n\nKay explains that a burner or stinger is a brief stretch or squeeze of the arm nerves. The burning often fades fast, but weakness can linger or appear later.\n\nWhat can help: recheck arm strength after the game and the next morning, sit out the rest of the match if weakness, tingling or neck pain remain, get the neck assessed after repeat episodes, and build neck and shoulder-blade strength alongside safer tackling technique.\n\nGet emergency help if both arms or a leg are affected, there's midline neck tenderness, the neck can't move, or someone was knocked out.\n\nOur Sydney CBD and Chatswood physios can help. Book via the link in bio.\n\nGeneral information only — not a substitute for an individual assessment.",
